  "id": "COMPOUND:14726 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Fluticasone, through its interaction with OVCAR-5 cells, appears to exert a target-directed influence on the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, as evidenced by multiple pathways. The shared target of OVCAR-5 with three different compounds—3-(5-Benzyloxy-3-methylpent-3-enyl)-2,2-dimethyloxirane, Chakasaponin Ii, and Terricollene B—suggests a potential mechanism where fluticasone may act as a modulator or activator of these compounds, which in turn target the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles implies a possible functional relationship between fluticasone and these molecules, possibly through a common mechanism of action or a shared biological pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that fluticasone may influence the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit via a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially involving receptor engagement or enzymatic modulation.",
